    "atom::4bf70b77dee00c619dca4fd4": {
      "atom_id": "atom::4bf70b77dee00c619dca4fd4",
      "source_handle": "P0364",
      "field_path": [
        "local_passages"
      ],
      "value": {
        "external_calls": 0,
        "passages": [
          {
            "best_sentence": "ency, and link thickness represents co-occurrence strength.Earlieremerging terms are predominantly associated with specific immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) agents (e.g., ipilimumab, pembrolizumab), treatment modifiers (e.g., antibiotics, proton pump inhibitors), and outcome-oriented concepts (e.g., overall survival, progression-free survival).More recent terms cluster around microbiome modulation strategies (e.g., fecal microbiota transplantation, microbial metabolites) and advanced profiling techniques (e.g., metagenomics, metabolomics), illustrating the temporal evolution of research priorities within the gut microbiome-immune checkpoint inhibitor field from foundational outcome studies toward targeted interventions.",
            "card_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\paper_cards\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\reading\\cards\\9dd62eb058feb9dbd44c28e9c8d004181dd8d19d\\087ed47cfe6952f4d934d87e8dd43399\\attempt-01\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json",
            "doi": "10.3389/fimmu.2026.1883259",
            "limits": [],
            "match_terms": [
              "微生物组",
              "抗生素",
              "质子泵抑制剂",
              "gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours",
              "ici"
            ],
            "material_depth": "fulltext",
            "paper_id": "9dd62eb058feb9dbd44c28e9c8d004181dd8d19d",
            "pool_action": "already_in_pool",
            "reading_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\paper_cards\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\materials\\9dd62eb058feb9dbd44c28e9c8d004181dd8d19d\\snapshot-eb0632c06695c138d8c4eef1",
            "score": 49.151244,
            "section_path": [
              "FIGURE 3"
            ],
            "segment_kind": "document_block",
            "source_handle": "P0364",
            "text": "2023.5).Node size reflects keyword frequency, and link thickness represents co-occurrence strength.Earlieremerging terms are predominantly associated with speci ency, and link thickness represents co-occurrence strength.Earlieremerging terms are predominantly associated with specific immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) agents (e.g., ipilimumab, pembrolizumab), treatment modifiers (e.g., antibiotics, proton pump inhibitors), and outcome-oriented concepts (e.g., overall survival, progression-free survival).More recent terms cluster around microbiome modulation strategies (e.g., fecal microbiota transplantation, microbial metabolites) and advanced profiling techniques (e.g., metagenomics, metabolomics), illustrating the temporal evolution of research priorities within the gut microbiome-immune checkpoint inhibitor field from foundational outcome studies toward targeted interventions. (11) and Gopalakrishnan et al.",
            "title": "Functional convergence amid taxonomic variability in gut microbiome–immune checkpoint inhibitor research: a bibliometric and mechanistic synthesis",
            "usable_fields": [],
            "year": "2026"
          }
        ],
        "question": "How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect? 外部因素对微生物 - 免疫轴的干扰 评估抗生素、PPIs、饮食等外部因素如何通过改变微生物组进而影响 ICI 疗效，特别是时间窗口和药物类别的特异性。 涵盖抗生素、质子泵抑制剂、其他合并用药（阿片类、类固醇、二甲双胍等）、饮食模式、生活方式（睡眠、节律）对 ICI 疗效的观察性关联证据及潜在机制。明确区分观察性关联与因果推断，标注肿瘤类型特异性及混杂因素限制。",
        "reading_mode": "focused_local_search"
      },
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::09453c46fe36046e2b9f48ff6256228cf0dc85f082eb8d8faf50756318235919",
